node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T19:14:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T19:14:08Z","body":"tbh you can just set ratio as an expression (`16.0/9`).\r\nEither way, having 2 properties doing the same is rather redundant, unless both of them have some advantages. What's the use for `ratio`?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833600267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833717741","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105820#issuecomment-2833717741","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105820","id":2833717741,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o5xnt","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T00:17:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T00:17:00Z","body":"> I don't see why both properties can't coexist instead of one needing to be deprecated\r\n\r\nAs explained in OP, using the `float` version usually gives unexpected results, so the use should be discouraged.\r\n\r\nFor example, a `HBoxContainer` being `640x359.995` will make its children one pixel shorter than expected. [MRP](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19932469/aspect.zip)\r\n\r\n> tbh you can just set ratio as an expression (16.0/9)\r\n\r\nYes, that's exactly what I did. But the calculation happens in the editor, it's still stored as a `1.7778`, the error is still there.\r\n\r\n> having 2 properties doing the same is rather redundant, unless both of them have some advantages.\r\n\r\nFor compatibility.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833717741/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2834599020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105820#issuecomment-2834599020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105820","id":2834599020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o9Ixs","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T09:30:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T09:30:56Z","body":"While I think the precision issue is indeed a problem, I think it would likely be better to provide a way to increase the precision of the stored value instead of working things around this way. This could involve transforming the value into another type internally (I guess either a 64bit integer or whatever works), and use the aspect ratio value.\r\n\r\nBut in any case, there's no way around having some precision issues at some point. If pixel-accuracy matters, then instead we should provide a way to have a pixel-perfect positioning (via a settings maybe). But TBH, I think GUI elements should always be pixel-aligned anyways, at least for Containers. So maybe we can just round the values for the Container's child's position and size right away instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2834599020/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2834620917","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105820#issuecomment-2834620917","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105820","id":2834620917,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o9OH1","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T09:39:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T09:39:25Z","body":"The precision can be increased by specifying a custom step for the property, which overrides the inspector's default precision.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2834620917/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2834628097","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105820#issuecomment-2834628097","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105820","id":2834628097,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o9P4B","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T09:42:19Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T09:42:19Z","body":"> I think it would likely be better to provide a way to increase the precision of the stored value instead of working things around this way\r\n\r\nThere's always been a recurring issue of the editor fiddling with a float property's value and snapping it by some arbitrary value (by default `0.001` as by editor settings), making working with precise floats very difficult with no way to increase it on a case-by-case basis. I think this new property is a bit of a band-aid for the bigger issue I described.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2834628097/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2835532449","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105820#issuecomment-2835532449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105820","id":2835532449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pAsqh","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T14:55:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T14:55:53Z","body":"I have the same problem in my game.\r\nI belive an option to round the number would be a good solution too.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2835532449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]